From 4f96c058b13ed1186fb30fecb03bcfc1a06cc7ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "D. Zack Garza" <dzackgarza@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 01:13:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/16] fix: give each Lean checkout its own package overrides
 instead of failing

Lake fixes a project's packages directory in its lakefile and records it in the
manifest: "-K packagesDir=" is ignored, and a lakefile whose packagesDir
disagrees with its manifest is rejected as out of date. The path therefore
cannot be overridden per project, and with one shared directory two checkouts
pinning one package at different revisions could not both resolve -- which the
previous script reported and refused.

The pins stay as they are and neither checkout is dropped. The shared packages
directory carries the packages the checkouts agree on, and provisioning writes
/opt/lake-views/index.json: per checkout, the packages pinned at a revision the
shared directory does not hold, each naming its content-addressed checkout under
/opt/lake-packages. `docker/sage-image.py run --lean-view CHECKOUT` mounts
exactly those over the packages directory for that invocation, so each run sees
its own manifest, no global symlink is rewritten, and the checkouts keep their
pins.

Verified concurrently in the published unpacked image: lean-cas-dsl (no flag)
and lean-cas-dsl-leaf-contracts (--lean-view) reported their own lean_categories
revisions -- eea5c7f3... and 82d1370d... -- while both imported Mathlib
("Nat.add_comm : forall (n m : Nat), n + m = m + n"), exit 0.

Not part of this change: an interrupted experiment that relocated Mathlib's
build tree into the content-addressed checkout. Its outputs were restored from
the official cache (lake exe cache get, 8322 oleans) and nothing is moved now.
